# P2P Validation

This document describes the conceptual validation network that the repository is prepared to support in the future.

## Conceptual flow

```text
Creator
   ↓
Validator A
Validator B
Validator C
   ↓
Evidence
   ↓
Audit
   ↓
Counter-Audit
   ↓
Revalidation
```

## Purpose

P2P validation is intended to reduce the risk that a single validator or a single authority becomes a permanent source of truth.

## Governance constraints

This repository does not implement:
- blockchain;
- cryptocurrency;
- token economics;
- wallet-based validation;
- automatic authority transfer.

The repository is not a crypto project.

## Operational meaning

P2P validation is a conceptual model for independent review and evidence-based challenge. It is compatible with the repository’s trust model, which includes skepticism, traceability, and revalidation.

## Important rule

No validator becomes permanently trusted simply by being a validator.

A validation record remains re-evaluable and contestable.

